name non-decimal-units
category Package
revision 69742
shortdesc Display and manipulate historical non-decimal units
relocated 1
longdesc Many historical unit systems were non-decimal. For example, the
longdesc Danish rigsdaler -- where 1 rigsdaler consists of 6 mark, each
longdesc again consisting of 16 skilling for a total of 96 skilling per
longdesc rigsdaler -- was used from 1625 to 1875, when currency was
longdesc decimalised to the current system of 1 krone = 100 ore. Units
longdesc for such measures as length, area, weight, and so on were also
longdesc often non-decimal, and in fact remain so in the few places of
longdesc the world that have not made the change to the metric system.
longdesc The non-decimal numbers were chosen due to their larger number
longdesc of division factors, which simplified mental arithmetic, eg.
longdesc when sharing an amount of money or dividing goods. This package
longdesc enables creation and configuration of such units to facilitate
longdesc their presentation in textual and tabular contexts, as well as
longdesc simple arithmetic.
runfiles size=8
